# tech-route-maker Cursor Rule

When the user asks for a technical route diagram, paper framework figure, publication figure, engineering route, method flowchart, roadmap, workflow, pipeline, or editable diagram output:

1. Read `SKILL.md`.
2. Build or update `tech-route.json` before rendering.
3. Inventory sources and record stable IDs, locators and SHA-256 hashes.
4. Offer the closest preset, then confirm missing domain and final delivery choices.
5. Run strict validation before final rendering; inference and unresolved questions are draft-only.
6. Report `QUALITY_REPORT.md` findings and required manual revision.
7. Keep PPTX/SVG/Draw.io/Excalidraw outputs editable; do not use screenshots as the main artifact.
8. If the user asks for copyable Draw.io or diagrams.net code, include `drawio-code` and explain how to paste `tech-route.drawio-code.xml` into [diagrams.net / draw.io](https://app.diagrams.net/) through **Extras > Edit Diagram**.

Use one concise grouped question rather than guessing final choices.
